   * Molality (m) — temperature independent', '[]', '', '[]', '[]', 'This chapter covers liquid solutions (mainly binary), their formation, concentration expressions, solubility factors (especially gases via Henry\'s law), vapor pressure (Raoult\'s law), ideal/non-ideal behavior, colligative properties, and abnormal molar masses due to association/dissociation (van\'t Hoff factor). It emphasizes that most life processes occur in solutions and links properties to the number of solute particles rather than their nature (colligative properties).
